WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.189 --> 00:00:01.855
- So migraine headaches are actually

00:00:01.855 --> 00:00:04.590
a lot more common than
many people might think,

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:08.223
and I get migraines as do
12% of the US population.

00:00:08.223 --> 00:00:11.321
So this video is me
looking into some treatment

00:00:11.321 --> 00:00:14.984
for migraines and it involves
some needles in the head.

00:00:14.984 --> 00:00:16.811
So if you are a little squeamish

00:00:16.811 --> 00:00:17.990
and this isn't your thing,

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.119
then you probably don't
wanna watch this video.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:21.119
Just saying.

00:00:25.194 --> 00:00:28.104
So the exact cause of migraines
is not fully understood

00:00:28.104 --> 00:00:29.859
but the symptoms are described as,

00:00:29.859 --> 00:00:31.882
"Excruciating pain that
is throbbing or pulsing,

00:00:31.882 --> 00:00:34.732
blurred vision, extreme
sensitivity to light,

00:00:34.732 --> 00:00:36.398
fatigue, nausea, and vomiting."

00:00:36.398 --> 00:00:37.830
There are preventive things you can do

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:38.750
and there are treatments,

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.852
but for a lot of people like myself

00:00:39.852 --> 00:00:41.222
these things don't always work.

00:00:41.222 --> 00:00:43.213
And for me recently my
migraines have been increasing

00:00:43.213 --> 00:00:45.035
so I was talking to my doctor about it,

00:00:45.035 --> 00:00:46.934
and he had suggested me looking in

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.742
to putting a neurotoxin into my head.

00:00:49.742 --> 00:00:51.154
This is like botox.

00:00:51.154 --> 00:00:52.916
Now, though this does not sound like

00:00:52.916 --> 00:00:54.556
the most pleasant thing in the world,

00:00:54.556 --> 00:00:56.717
it's actually something
I'm willing to consider

00:00:56.717 --> 00:00:58.056
because I do have some experience

00:00:58.056 --> 00:01:00.054
with injections into my scalp

00:01:00.054 --> 00:01:01.966
because of my autoimmune disorder.

00:01:01.966 --> 00:01:02.799
Before the procedure,

00:01:02.799 --> 00:01:04.807
I asked family friend and respected doctor

00:01:04.807 --> 00:01:07.529
Doctor Henning of Princeton
Dermatology Associates,

00:01:07.529 --> 00:01:09.999
to explain how exactly botox is thought

00:01:09.999 --> 00:01:11.393
to help migraine pain.

00:01:11.393 --> 00:01:12.949
- The mechanism of action for botox

00:01:12.949 --> 00:01:15.950
in the treatment of migraines
is not fully understood.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.347
The neurotoxin paralyzes muscles

00:01:18.347 --> 00:01:20.458
and it is thought that
its use in migraines

00:01:20.458 --> 00:01:22.531
is related to pain transmission

00:01:22.531 --> 00:01:24.616
that is reduced when
you paralyze the muscles

00:01:24.616 --> 00:01:25.632
around the head.

00:01:25.632 --> 00:01:27.247
- So we talked to Doctor Henning

00:01:27.247 --> 00:01:29.128
and I think I'm gonna go for it.

00:01:29.128 --> 00:01:32.216
I'm still a little nervous
about some of the risks

00:01:32.216 --> 00:01:34.021
but it seems to be something

00:01:34.021 --> 00:01:35.687
that helps a lot of people.

00:01:35.687 --> 00:01:37.736
So we're gonna give it shot.

00:01:37.736 --> 00:01:38.569
- Should be interesting.

00:01:38.569 --> 00:01:39.464
- It should be interesting.

00:01:39.464 --> 00:01:40.297
- Yeah!
- Yeah.

00:01:40.297 --> 00:01:42.590
And so it was time for the appointment

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:44.918
but first they cleaned my head a lot.

00:01:44.918 --> 00:01:47.218
Next the doctor had me wrinkle my forehead

00:01:47.218 --> 00:01:49.453
and marked the injection spots.

00:01:49.453 --> 00:01:51.236
And now time for the botox.

00:01:51.236 --> 00:01:53.986
(electric music)

00:02:04.545 --> 00:02:07.527
The botox as a numbing
agent is pretty incredible.

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.331
Surprisingly despite how this looks,

00:02:09.331 --> 00:02:11.664
the process was pretty mild.

00:02:13.077 --> 00:02:15.769
And in just 15 minutes it was over.

00:02:15.769 --> 00:02:17.191
Two days later,

00:02:17.191 --> 00:02:18.909
I didn't notice much of a difference.

00:02:18.909 --> 00:02:20.142
My face could still wrinkle

00:02:20.142 --> 00:02:23.809
and I even had a minor
migraine on day four.

00:02:25.109 --> 00:02:26.421
Five days later.

00:02:26.421 --> 00:02:29.144
My face feels relaxed in a weird way

00:02:29.144 --> 00:02:32.209
and the forehead wrinkles have smoothed.

00:02:32.209 --> 00:02:34.966
Three weeks later: final thoughts.

00:02:34.966 --> 00:02:37.886
I would say that the overall
experience was unexpected.

00:02:37.886 --> 00:02:38.831
When looking up botox

00:02:38.831 --> 00:02:41.422
I found two very opposite search results.

00:02:41.422 --> 00:02:43.993
Half of what I saw were
more like botox ads

00:02:43.993 --> 00:02:46.112
where people just looked ecstatic

00:02:46.112 --> 00:02:47.584
to be getting shots in their head.

00:02:47.584 --> 00:02:51.219
The other half I found were
tons of horrific photos.

00:02:51.219 --> 00:02:52.879
Their eyebrows stuck up here,

00:02:52.879 --> 00:02:55.399
their faces frozen in
this really weird way.

00:02:55.399 --> 00:02:58.871
My actual experience is
simply a boring middle-ground.

00:02:58.871 --> 00:03:01.089
The process was easier
than I had expected.

00:03:01.089 --> 00:03:03.531
I haven't had a migraine since day four,

00:03:03.531 --> 00:03:06.685
and I am loving this
wrinkle free forehead.

00:03:06.685 --> 00:03:09.191
Actually there are some
serious things to be aware of.

00:03:09.191 --> 00:03:10.024
You can actually get something

00:03:10.024 --> 00:03:11.697
where your eyelid completely droops,

00:03:11.697 --> 00:03:13.615
you can hit like a major blood vessel

00:03:13.615 --> 00:03:14.448
or something like that.

00:03:14.448 --> 00:03:16.100
I mean there are some actual complications

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:16.959
that can happen.

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:18.614
While I'm appreciative of everything,

00:03:18.614 --> 00:03:19.623
I feel very fortunate

00:03:19.623 --> 00:03:21.234
that I have access to something like this,

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.619
it's still nothing to take lightly.

00:03:22.619 --> 00:03:24.570
So that's my review;

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:28.386
boring and in the middle
but hopefully it's helpful.

00:03:28.386 --> 00:03:29.219
Look at that!

00:03:29.219 --> 00:03:30.489
Look at how ecstatic they are!

00:03:30.489 --> 00:03:32.156
Amy you see how happy they are?

00:03:32.156 --> 00:03:32.989
- [Amy] They are loving it.

00:03:32.989 --> 00:03:34.278
- They are loving it.

00:03:34.278 --> 00:03:36.111
Who are these people?!

